description:
pkix-lint/src/deviation.rs:322:

    pub struct DeviationScope {
        pub kind: String,
        pub props: Vec<(String, ScopePropValue)>,
    }

The canonical kinds are `pub const SCOPE_KIND_*: &str` values — string
literals living in .rodata. But every constructor at lines 338-411
allocates a new String for `kind`:

    pub fn any() -> Self {
        Self {
            kind: SCOPE_KIND_ANY.to_string(),  // ← allocation
            props: Vec::new(),
        }
    }

    pub fn issuer_dn_contains(substring: impl Into<String>) -> Self {
        Self {
            kind: SCOPE_KIND_ISSUER_DN_CONTAINS.to_string(),  // ← allocation
            props: vec![(
                PROP_ISSUER_DN_SUBSTRING.to_string(),  // ← allocation
                ScopePropValue::Text(substring.into()),
            )],
        }
    }

For a deviation store with N entries, this is N+ (one per scope) gratuitous
String allocations. The props names are also String when they're always
one of the four canonical PROP_* constants.

# What the caller pays

For a deployment with a deviation pack of, say, 200 deviations, this is
~600 `&'static str → String` allocations just to model the canonical
kinds and props names. None of those Strings are ever mutated.

# What's leaking

The struct's type signature `pub kind: String` is part of the public
API. It locks the contract to 'kind is an owned heap string,' which
prevents:

  - Comparing kind with `== SCOPE_KIND_ANY` without `.as_str()` (works,
    but still requires the allocation in the first place).
  - Future migration to `Cow<'static, str>` (zero-cost for canonical
    kinds, allocating only for custom kinds) without a breaking
    change.

The recent Cow<'static, str> migration for LintResult detail
(PKIX-ua6q) addressed the same shape. The same pattern applies here:
canonical kinds known at compile time get Borrowed; custom kinds get
Owned.

# Suggested fix

Change to:

    pub struct DeviationScope {
        pub kind: Cow<'static, str>,
        pub props: Vec<(Cow<'static, str>, ScopePropValue)>,
    }

And constructors:

    pub fn any() -> Self {
        Self {
            kind: Cow::Borrowed(SCOPE_KIND_ANY),
            props: Vec::new(),
        }
    }

    pub fn issuer_dn_contains(substring: impl Into<String>) -> Self {
        Self {
            kind: Cow::Borrowed(SCOPE_KIND_ISSUER_DN_CONTAINS),
            props: vec![(
                Cow::Borrowed(PROP_ISSUER_DN_SUBSTRING),
                ScopePropValue::Text(substring.into()),
            )],
        }
    }

Custom kinds still use `Cow::Owned` and pay one allocation, same as
today. Canonical kinds pay zero.

This is a public-field type change, breaking change pre-1.0. Free to
make.

# Why P3

Allocation cost is not significant in normal use (deviation stores
have hundreds of entries, not millions). The fix is structurally
clean but the immediate impact is small. Worth pinning before 1.0;
not urgent.
